    <node id="Philo">
      <data key="d0">Philo</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Philo is a topological node in an electrical power network that functions as a key connectivity point for both transmission elements and equipment. It serves as an endpoint for multiple AC transmission line segments, including AC Line Segment 45-49, AC Line Segment 49-51, AC Line Segment 49-54, AC Line Segment 49-66, AC Line Segment 49-69, and AC Line Segment 42-49. Through these connections, the topological node Philo links various portions of the AC transmission system and participates in the broader power network topology.

In addition to its role as a junction for AC line segments, the topological node Philo is also the connection point for specific pieces of equipment. The synchronous machine named Philo SM is connected to this node, indicating that generation or synchronous compensation is electrically tied into the network at Philo. Furthermore, the energy consumer designated Philo LD is connected at the same node, representing a load that draws power from the network at this location. Collectively, these characteristics define Philo as a significant node where multiple AC transmission lines, a synchronous machine, and an energy consumer are all interconnected within the power system.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-018</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781189737</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Glen Lyn">
      <data key="d0">Glen Lyn</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Glen Lyn is a topological node in an electrical power transmission network, specifically within a 132 kV system, that functions as a key connection point for multiple AC transmission line segments. It is consistently described as serving as one endpoint of several AC line segments, including AC Line Segment 92-100, AC Line Segment 98-100, AC Line Segment 99-100, AC Line Segment 100-103, and AC Line Segment 100-104.

As a topological node, Glen Lyn represents a bus or junction in the network where these AC lines meet, enabling the interconnection of different parts of the transmission system. Various descriptions emphasize that Glen Lyn is connected by AC transmission lines or AC line segments in general, underscoring its role as a critical node through which power flows between multiple segments of the grid.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-028</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781189738</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tidd1">
      <data key="d0">Tidd1</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Tidd1 is a topological node in an electrical power transmission network that represents a network connection point. It functions as a bus or node where different elements of the power system are electrically connected.

Tidd1 is connected by AC transmission lines, including serving as one endpoint of specific AC line segments identified as AC Line Segment 54-59 and AC Line Segment 56-59. It also connects to another network location referred to as Sunnysde, indicating its role as part of the broader transmission topology.

In addition to its line connections, Tidd1 is the node to which a synchronous machine, referred to as Tidd Sm or Tidd SM, is connected. Through this synchronous machine connection and its role as an endpoint of multiple AC line segments, Tidd1 serves as a key electrical junction within the power network.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5b7511181d9d21111b49ecee6f4b82f-chunk-040</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781189738</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TwinBrch">
      <data key="d0">TwinBrch</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">TwinBrch is a topological node in an electrical power network, specifically within a 132 kV system, that functions as a key connection point for multiple AC line segments and an associated load. As a topological node, TwinBrch represents a bus or junction where various elements of the network are electrically connected and can be analyzed as a single point in network topology.

TwinBrch serves as one endpoint of AC Line Segment 12-14 in the 132 kV network, and it is also connected to several other AC line segments, including Line Segment 3-12, Line Segment 7-12, Line Segment 11-12, and Line Segment 12-16. Through these multiple line connections, TwinBrch acts as an important node for power transfer and network connectivity within the transmission system.

In addition to its role as a junction for AC transmission lines, TwinBrch is connected to an energy consumer entity named TwinBrch LD. This indicates that the node not only supports through-flow of power along transmission lines but also supplies electrical energy to a local load associated with TwinBrch LD. Together, these characteristics define TwinBrch as a significant topological node integrating both transmission paths and consumption within the electrical network.</data>
